%U A398946 8,7,0,2,7,1,2,4,3,2,7,5,0,4,4,4,1,2,3,4,8,5
%N A398946 Decimal expansion of the dihedral angle, in radians, between any two adjacent faces in a canonical (dual-uniform) 10-gonal trapezohedron.
%C A398946 The 10-gonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the 10-gonal antiprism.
%H A398946 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398946/b398946.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398946 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Decagonal_antitegum">Decagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398946 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%F A398946 Equals arccos((2 - 3*sqrt(5) - 2*sqrt(125 + 38*sqrt(5)))/41).
%F A398946 Equals arccos(c), where c = -0.82168... is the smallest root of 41*x^4 - 8*x^3 - 26*x^2 + 8*x + 1.
%e A398946 2.5351507732236044986524236031023726483833011876696...
%t A398946 First[RealDigits[ArcCos[(2 - Sqrt[45] - 2*Sqrt[125 + 38*Sqrt[5]])/41], 10, 100]]
%t A398946 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398946 First[RealDigits[First[PolyhedronData[{"Trapezohedron", 10}, "DihedralAngles"]], 10, 100]]
%Y A398946 Cf. A398938 (volume), A398939 (surface area), A398940 (inradius), A398941 (midradius), A398942 (height).
%Y A398946 Cf. A398943 (long edge).
%Y A398946 Cf. A398944 (small face angle), A398945 (large face angle).
